\cf0 Key hyperparams: learning rate, batch size, epochs, dropout rate. Tuning methods: Grid Search (exhaustive), Random Search (faster), Bayesian optimisation (smarter). Learning rate schedulers (warm-up + cosine decay) are standard in deep learning. Use MLflow to log all runs and compare.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Fine-tuning methods: Full fine-tuning (expensive), LoRA/QLoRA (efficient \'97 only tune low-rank adapters), PEFT (parameter-efficient). Steps: prepare instruction-tuned dataset 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  set learning rate (small: 1e-4 to 1e-5) 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  train with gradient checkpointing 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  evaluate with ROUGE, BLEU, or task-specific metrics. Use Hugging Face Trainer or Databricks MLflow.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
