\cf0 Overfitting = model performs well on training data but poorly on unseen data (high variance). Remedies: (1) More training data, (2) Regularisation \'97 L1 (Lasso, sparse features) or L2 (Ridge, smooth weights), (3) Dropout (for neural nets), (4) Cross-validation (k-fold), (5) Early stopping, (6) Simpler model architecture. Outliers are a data quality issue, not overfitting.}